title: 'Era points for blocks validators author on system chains'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Validators earn era points for the blocks they author on system chains, weighted per chain and
    service by governance.

    `sp-staking` gains `ValidatorServiceKind` (`RelayConsensus`, `Collation`) and `RewardPoints`,
    and now holds `RewardsReporter`, which `frame-support` re-exports at the same path.

    `pallet-staking-async` gains `reward_service_points`, which credits points for a service other
    than relay chain consensus to the active era, dropping accounts not exposed in it. Points also
    go to the new `ErasRewardPointsByService`, next to the unchanged combined tally. No migration.
    External `WeightInfo` implementors must add `reward_service_points`.

    `pallet-validator-collators` counts the blocks each author produces and reports the counts of
    the validators in the stored set every `ReportPeriod` blocks, and once per set shortly before
    the expected era end. New config items: `BlockReporter`, `DefaultReportPeriod`,
    `MaxEntriesPerReport`, `UnixTime`, `DefaultExpectedEraDuration`, `DefaultReportMargin` and
    `MaxReportMargin`. The runtime adds the pallet to the `EventHandler` of `pallet-authorship`.

    New `pallet-staking-async-points-converter`, for Asset Hub, converts the reported counts into
    era points using `PointsPerService`, set by governance.
